  "question": {
    "text": "From the following, the quantity (constructed from the basic constants of nature), that has the dimensions, as well as correct order of magnitude, vis-a-vis typical atomic size, is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "55h8h",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{e^2}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 m c^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "P8fvE",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 e^2}{m e^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BEBJy",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{m e^2}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 b^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "j1Rgb",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 m c^2}{e^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As $\\mathrm{E}=\\mathrm{mc}^2$\nalso $\\mathrm{E}=\\mathrm{F} \\cdot \\mathrm{s}=\\frac{\\mathrm{kq} \\cdot \\mathrm{q}}{\\mathrm{r}^2} \\cdot \\mathrm{r}$\nTherefore dimensionally\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{mc}^2=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\epsilon_0} \\frac{\\mathrm{q}^2}{\\mathrm{r}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{r}=\\frac{\\mathrm{e}^2}{4 \\pi \\epsilon_0 \\mathrm{mc}^2}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
